      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Consult your doctor before starting magnesium supplements because kidney disease alters how your body processes this mineral, and excessive intake can lead to dangerous side effects. While typical supplemental doses range from 200 to 400 mg, your specific stage two condition requires a personalized prescription rather than a standard \"quick relief\" dose. Taking more than your kidney doctor recommends—even for simple nighttime cramps—can cause fluid buildup or interfere with kidney function, which could worsen your condition. Please prioritize a conversation with your nephrologist to determine a safe dosage that addresses your symptoms without compromising your health.",
